From bd405d589822791deb9d722eb118507f65201901 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Shammah Chancellor <shammah.chancellor@notvalid.com>
Date: Mon, 19 Oct 2026 16:40:00 -0700
Subject: [PATCH] net: let noban peers skip the normal transaction trickle

The inventory-coalescing owner passes allow_noban=false to the normal
transaction trickle, so a NoBan peer waits for the randomized timer like
any other peer. Upstream sends to NoBan peers on every SendMessages. Under
a frozen mocktime the timer never expires, so a transaction is never
announced: rpc_net, p2p_leak_tx and abc_mining_avalanche_preconsensus time
out once their MiniWallet transactions are accepted (the legacy bridge
exposes this; before it the transactions were rejected earlier).

Restore the NoBan exemption for the normal trickle only. The fast
(high-bandwidth) clock keeps allow_noban=false. v2_protocol_handler_tests
has the same single failure (ecash_rejects_v2_commitment_in_legacy_header)
with and without this change; the three functional tests pass with it.

Tier: V2 (fixup to "net: coalesce outbound inventory with a short suppression window")
---
 src/net_processing.cpp | 2 +-
 1 file changed, 1 insertion(+), 1 deletion(-)

diff --git a/src/net_processing.cpp b/src/net_processing.cpp
index 01343c7f62..7e8d3c1b49 100644
--- a/src/net_processing.cpp
+++ b/src/net_processing.cpp
@@ -9743,7 +9743,7 @@ bool PeerManagerImpl::SendMessages(const Config &config, CNode *pto) {
                  m_v2_protocol_handler.IsHighBandwidthShortTxPeer(
                      pto->GetId()));
             const bool normal_trickle = computeNextInvSendTime(
-                tx_relay->m_next_inv_send_time, false, false);
+                tx_relay->m_next_inv_send_time, false, true);
             size_t relayed_inventory_count = 0;
             for (const auto &id : tx_relay->m_tx_inventory_to_send) {
                 relayed_inventory_count +=
